      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m trying to decide whether we should notify before or after calling the callback... I think the issue with doing it before the callback is that we could have a success status in the callback, then race such that the buffer is now unmapped in the callback scope which might assume that the buffer should be successfully mapped.\n\nI think it might be safer to notify after calling the callback? WDYT?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 317,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f1e05f859bdd91f1b567c732bcc41b8395fb9c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ade73f8a_ed72c9b7",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1004831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T18:14:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "At ToT the MapAsyncEvent mutex is released after FinalizeMap() runs but before the callback runs so that is already a problem.\n\nEven if you change this to notify after the callback returns, if timing changes slightly and APIUnmap() runs immediately after mState changes to Mapped then Unmap() will start on regular path. Unmap() will happen immediately and the buffer might be unmapped by the time the callback does something like GetMappedPtr() on a different thread.\n\nI think we can rely on calls to buffer being externally synchronized? If the application intentionally unmaps a buffer pending map it should have somehow cancelled the map async callback so it won\u0027t use the buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "fc045bfa_340f041e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 317,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f1e05f859bdd91f1b567c732bcc41b8395fb9c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "355ba9ed_69248b68",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 318,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-11-06T19:23:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm would it work if we had an additional `atomic\u003cbool\u003e` or something that we wait on in the `Buffer` that signals whether the callback is complete? (On top of waiting for the state change?)\n\nI agree that in most cases we should be able to rely on buffers being externally synchronized, but I feel like it should be possible to guarantee synchronization for at least the callback since we schedule it.",
      "parentUuid": "ade73f8a_ed72c9b7",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 317,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "2f1e05f859bdd91f1b567c732bcc41b8395fb9c0",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c5c412ff_6640502d",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/Buffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
